$DIR/main.p:17:20: cannot pass &mk() to (*O).Drop (called when mk() is dropped), which keeps it after returning
    &mk() points into the temporary O that mk().n returns. The O made at
    main.p:17 is a temporary: nothing keeps it, so its object is dropped at the
    end of the statement. A view of the object may be passed to calls in that
    statement but may not outlive it. (*O).Drop (called when mk() is dropped)
    stores o in package variable keep (main.p:11), so &mk() would outlive the
    temporary.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Change (*O).Drop (called when mk() is dropped) to take a value or an owner,
    which it can keep: an owned[T] from new, a shared[T], or a library owner
    such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)
